"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkmy_website=globalThis.webpackChunkmy_website||[]).push([[6743],{900:n=>{n.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"Sprint 7","metadata":{"permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 7","source":"@site/blog/sprint7/sprint_7.md","title":"Sprint 7","description":"From: 2026-05-06","date":"2026-05-19T01:59:01.190Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"Sprint 7","title":"Sprint 7"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Sprint 6","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 6"}},"content":"**From**: 2026-05-06\\n\\n**To**: 2026-05-19\\n\\n**Scrum Master**: Catarina Ribeiro\\n\\n**Product Owner**: IEETA\\n\\n**Developers**: Marta Cruz, Mariana Marques, Beatriz Francisco, Matilde Rodrigues\\n\\nIn this sprint, our primary focus shifted towards system stabilization, quality assurance and deployment readiness. We dedicated significant effort to implementing comprehensive testing, analyzing and improving security and setting up robust CI/CD pipelines for the final deployment. Additionally, we focused on hardware-related tasks, specifically the calibration and building of the suit, while also finalizing the customization of the Keycloak pages.\\n\\n- Customizing keycloak pages\\n- Unit tests\\n- Scalability and performance tests\\n- Integration tests\\n- Analysis and improvement of security\\n- CI/CD Pipelines\\n- Deployment\\n- Suit calibration\\n- Suit building\\n- Update Microsite \\n\\n| Expected     | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 10       |\\n| Story Points | 55       |\\n\\n## Sprint Backlog\\n\\n| Task (KAN-\\\\*) | Description                 | Developer                                      | State | Story Points |\\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------ |\\n| KAN-43        | Customizing keycloak pages | Catarina Ribeiro | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-44        | Unit tests  | Matilde Rodrigues                  | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-45        | Scalability and performance tests | Mariana Marques and Marta Cruz                | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-46        | Integration tests | Catarina Ribeiro | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-47        | Analysis and improvement of security          | Marta Cruz            | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-48        | CI/CD Pipelines | Beatriz Francisco | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-49        | Deployment | Beatriz Francisco | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-50        | Suit calibration | Marta Cruz and Beatriz Francisco | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-51        | Suit building | All | Not Done  | 10      |\\n| KAN-16        | Update Microsite            | Catarina Ribeiro            | Done  | 5          |\\n\\n### Task Status (Completed/Not Completed)\\n\\n- [x] KAN-43: Customizing keycloak pages\\n- [x] KAN-44: Unit tests\\n- [x] KAN-45: Scalability and performance tests\\n- [x] KAN-46: Integration tests\\n- [x] KAN-47: Analysis and improvement of security\\n- [x] KAN-48: CI/CD Pipelines\\n- [x] KAN-49: Deployment\\n- [x] KAN-50: Suit calibration\\n- [ ] KAN-51: Suit building\\n- [x] KAN-16: Update Microsite\\n\\n## Sprint Review\\n\\n| Concluded    | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 9        |\\n| Story Points | 45       |\\n\\n## Sprint Retrospective\\n\\nDuring this sprint, the team successfully executed a heavy workload focused on testing, security enhancements and deployment infrastructure. We achieved our main goals regarding software stability by completing all testing phases and successfully setting up the CI/CD pipelines and deployment. The team also successfully finished the suit calibration and Keycloak customization. The only task that was not concluded was \\"Suit building\\", which will be carried over to the next sprint so the we can finish it, since it\'s a time-consuming task. Overall, the team delivered 9 out of 10 tasks, demonstrating a strong pace and ensuring a robust foundation for the system\'s finalization.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e`"},{"id":"Sprint 6","metadata":{"permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 6","source":"@site/blog/sprint6/sprint_6.md","title":"Sprint 6","description":"From: 2026-04-01","date":"2026-05-04T23:55:38.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"Sprint 6","title":"Sprint 6"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Sprint 7","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 7"},"nextItem":{"title":"Sprint 5","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 5"}},"content":"**From**: 2026-04-01\\n\\n**To**: 2026-05-05\\n\\n**Scrum Master**: Beatriz Francisco\\n\\n**Product Owner**: IEETA\\n\\n**Developers**: Marta Cruz, Mariana Marques, Matilde Rodrigues, Catarina Ribeiro\\n\\nIn this sprint, our primary focus was to complete the remaining tasks from the previous sprint and continue the final system deployments. Additionally, we proceeded with the integration of multi-sensor support, expanding it to 7 sensors.\\n\\n- Researcher analysis\\n- Keycloak implementation\\n- Implementation of 7 sensores\\n- Chatbot implementation\\n- PWA suport implementation\\n- Smartwatch integration\\n- Update Microsite\\n\\n| Expected     | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 7        |\\n| Story Points | 50       |\\n\\n## Sprint Backlog\\n\\n| Task (KAN-\\\\*) | Description                 | Developer                                      | State | Story Points |\\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------ |\\n| KAN-35        | Researcher analysis | Beatriz Francisco and Mariana Marques  | Done  | 10      |\\n| KAN-38        | Keycloak implementation  | Marta Cruz                     | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-39        | Implementation of 7 sensores | Marta Cruz                | Done  | 10          |\\n| KAN-40        | Chatbot implementation | Beatriz Francisco and Matilde Rodrigues | Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-41        | PWA suport implementation           | Catarina Ribeiro            | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-42        | Smartwatch integration | Mariana Marques  | Not Done  | 10      |\\n| KAN-16        | Update Microsite            | Catarina Ribeiro            | Done  | 5          |\\n\\n### Task Status (Completed/Not Completed)\\n\\n- [x] KAN-35: Researcher analysis\\n- [x] KAN-38: Keycloak implementation \\n- [x] KAN-39: Implementation of 7 sensores\\n- [x] KAN-40: Chatbot implementation\\n- [x] KAN-41: PWA suport implementation\\n- [ ] KAN-42: Smartwatch integration\\n- [x] KAN-16: Update Microsite\\n\\n## Sprint Review\\n\\n| Concluded    | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 5        |\\n| Story Points | 40       |\\n\\n## Sprint Retrospective\\n\\nDuring this sprint, the team successfully focused on finalizing system deployments, completing pending work, and expanding multi-sensor support. As planned, tasks Researcher analysis and Keycloak implementation, which were initiated ahead of schedule in the previous sprint, were fully completed. Similarly, work on Smartwatch integration began during this sprint, but it is intentionally scheduled to be finished in the upcoming sprint. Overall, the team delivered 6 out of 7 tasks and achieved 40 story points, successfully meeting the sprint\'s core objectives and maintaining steady progress.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e`"},{"id":"Sprint 5","metadata":{"permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 5","source":"@site/blog/sprint5/sprint_5.md","title":"Sprint 5","description":"From: 2026-03-18","date":"2026-03-30T23:34:02.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"Sprint 5","title":"Sprint 5"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Sprint 6","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 6"},"nextItem":{"title":"Sprint 4","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 4"}},"content":"**From**: 2026-03-18\\n\\n**To**: 2026-03-31\\n\\n**Scrum Master**: Matilde Rodrigues\\n\\n**Product Owner**: IEETA\\n\\n**Developers**: Marta Cruz, Mariana Marques, Beatriz Francisco, Catarina Ribeiro\\n\\nIn this sprint, our primary focus was refining the current prototype for the upcoming milestone demonstration by refining existing features and improving user navigation. Additionally, we initiated the integration of multi-sensor support to expand the system\u2019s core capabilities.\\n\\n- Second sensor implementation\\n- Researcher analysis\\n- Extra page for the session history\\n- Gamification improvement\\n- Keycloak implementation\\n- Update Microsite\\n\\n| Expected     | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 6        |\\n| Story Points | 40       |\\n\\n## Sprint Backlog\\n\\n| Task (KAN-\\\\*) | Description                 | Developer                                      | State | Story Points |\\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------ |\\n| KAN-34        | Second sensor implementation  | Marta Cruz                | Done  | 10          |\\n| KAN-35        | Researcher analysis | Beatriz Francisco and Mariana Marques  | Not Done  | 10      |\\n| KAN-36        | Extra page for the session history | Catarina Ribeiro     | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-37        | Gamification improvement  | Matilde Rodrigues             | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-38        | Keycloak implementation  | Marta Cruz                     | Not Done  | 5      |\\n| KAN-16        | Update Microsite            | Catarina Ribeiro            | Done  | 5          |\\n\\n### Task Status (Completed/Not Completed)\\n\\n- [x] KAN-34: Second sensor implementation\\n- [ ] KAN-35: Researcher analysis\\n- [x] KAN-36: Extra page for the session history\\n- [x] KAN-37: Gamification improvement\\n- [ ] KAN-38: Keycloak implementation \\n- [x] KAN-16: Update Microsite\\n\\n## Sprint Review\\n\\n| Concluded    | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 4        |\\n| Story Points | 25       |\\n\\n## Sprint Retrospective\\n\\nThe team focused heavily on stabilizing the current prototype for the upcoming milestone, ensuring all user-facing features were functional and improving some of them. Although the Keycloak and Researcher analysys were not completed, these tasks intentionally started ahead of schedule and will be finished in the next sprint as planned. Overall, the team delivered 4 out of 6 tasks, successfully achieving the sprint\'s core objectives.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e`"},{"id":"Sprint 4","metadata":{"permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 4","source":"@site/blog/sprint4/sprint_4.md","title":"Sprint 4","description":"From: 2026-02-09","date":"2026-03-17T00:16:28.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"Sprint 4","title":"Sprint 4"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Sprint 5","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Sprint 3","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 3"}},"content":"**From**: 2026-02-09\\n\\n**To**: 2026-03-17\\n\\n**Scrum Master**: Catarina Ribeiro\\n\\n**Product Owner**: IEETA\\n\\n**Developers**: Marta Cruz, Mariana Marques, Beatriz Francisco, Matilde Rodrigues\\n\\nIn this sprint, we continued the work from last semester, starting to implement more features with special attention to usability and accessibility, which are the main goals for the first milestone of this semester.\\n\\n- Dark mode\\n- Color blind mode\\n- Text-to-speech\\n- System security improvement\\n- Data analysis integration\\n- Data analysis alerts integration\\n- Goals and Gamification \\n- Usability tests and SUS analysis\\n- Frontend refactoring\\n- Update Microsite\\n\\n| Expected     | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 10       |\\n| Story Points | 65       |\\n\\n## Sprint Backlog\\n\\n| Task (KAN-\\\\*) | Description                 | Developer                                      | State | Story Points |\\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------ |\\n| KAN-25        | Dark mode        | Catarina Ribeiro                       | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-26        | Color blind mode | Catarina Ribeiro                       | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-27        | Text-to-speech   | Catarina Ribeiro                       | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-28        | System security improvement  | Marta Cruz                 | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-29        | Data analysis integration | Beatriz Francisco             | Done  | 10         |\\n| KAN-30        | Data analysis alerts integration       | Mariana Marques  | Done  | 10         |\\n| KAN-31        | Goals and Gamification  | Matilde Rodrigues               | Done  | 10         |\\n| KAN-32        | Usability tests and SUS analysis | Catarina Ribeiro and Marta Cruz            | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-33        | Frontend refactoring | Catarina Ribeiro                   | Done  | 5          |\\n| KAN-16        | Update Microsite            | Catarina Ribeiro            | Done  | 5          |\\n\\n### Task Status (Completed/Not Completed)\\n\\n- [x] KAN-25: Dark mode\\n- [x] KAN-26: Color blind mode\\n- [x] KAN-27: Text-to-Speech\\n- [x] KAN-28: System security improvement\\n- [x] KAN-29: Data analysis integration\\n- [x] KAN-30: Data analysis alerts integration\\n- [x] KAN-31: Goals and Gamification \\n- [x] KAN-32: Usability tests and SUS analysis\\n- [x] KAN-33: Frontend refactoring\\n- [x] KAN-16: Update Microsite\\n\\n## Sprint Review\\n\\n| Concluded    | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 10       |\\n| Story Points | 65       |\\n\\n## Sprint Retrospective\\n\\nThis sprint was focused and productive, with the team making significant progress on usability and accessibility features. The implementation of dark mode, color blind mode, and text-to-speech functionality marked important steps toward a more inclusive user experience, while the frontend refactoring helped improve the overall code maintainability. Furthermore, we successfully moved beyond the core milestone objectives by proactively advancing several integration and security tasks, putting the project ahead of the initial schedule.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e`"},{"id":"Sprint 3","metadata":{"permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 3","source":"@site/blog/sprint3/sprint_3.md","title":"Sprint 3","description":"From: 2025-11-19","date":"2025-12-16T22:29:37.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"Sprint 3","title":"Sprint 3"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Sprint 4","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 4"},"nextItem":{"title":"Sprint 2","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 2"}},"content":"**From**: 2025-11-19\\n\\n**To**: 2025-12-16\\n\\n**Scrum Master**: Beatriz Francisco\\n\\n**Product Owner**: IEETA\\n\\n**Developers**: Marta Cruz, Mariana Marques, Matilde Rodrigues, Catarina Ribeiro\\n\\nIn this sprint, we aimed to finish all tasks related to the MVP for the milestone 3 and also an extra task that was not planned for this semester. \\n\\n- Setup all four databases\\n- Complete backend API implementation\\n- Full Frontend-Backend API integration\\n- 3D Avatar & Data Simulation on Frontend\\n- Live Sensor Integration & Real-time Visualization\\n- Setup LaTeX Report\\n- Preparation for Third Presentation\\n- Update Microsite\\n\\n| Expected     | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 8        |\\n| Story Points | 40       |\\n\\n## Sprint Backlog\\n\\n| Task (KAN-\\\\*) | Description                 | Developer                                      | State | Story Points |\\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------ |\\n| KAN-18        | Setup all four databases   | Mariana Marques e Beatriz Francisco              | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-19        | Complete backend API implementation |  Catarina Ribeiro, Mariana Marques and Marta Cruz| Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-20        | Full Frontend-Backend API integration| All                                   | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-21        | 3D Avatar & Data Simulation on Frontend | Beatriz Francisco                  | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-22        | Live Sensor Integration & Real-time Visualization | Marta Cruz Francisco                           | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-23        | Setup LaTeX Report         | Matilde Rodrigues                              | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-24        | Preparation for Third Presentation | All                                     | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-16        | Update Microsite            | Catarina Ribeiro                               | Done  | 5            |\\n\\n### Task Status (Completed/Not Completed)\\n\\n- [x] KAN-18: Setup all four databases\\n- [x] KAN-19: Complete backend API implementation\\n- [x] KAN-20: Full Frontend-Backend API integration\\n- [x] KAN-21: 3D Avatar & Data Simulation on Frontend\\n- [x] KAN-22: Live Sensor Integration & Real-time Visualization\\n- [x] KAN-23: Setup LaTeX Report\\n- [x] KAN-24: Preparation for Third Presentation\\n- [x] KAN-16: Update Microsite\\n\\n## Sprint Review\\n\\n| Concluded    | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 8        |\\n| Story Points | 40       |\\n\\n## Sprint Retrospective\\n\\nThis sprint was intense but highly productive. The team successfully delivered all core components of Milestone 3, transforming the project from a conceptual model into a working prototype. The integration of the live sensor with the 3D visualization was a particular highlight and a significant technical success.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e`"},{"id":"Sprint 2","metadata":{"permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 2","source":"@site/blog/sprint2/sprint_2.md","title":"Sprint 2","description":"From: 2025-10-28","date":"2025-11-17T12:56:38.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"Sprint 2","title":"Sprint 2"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Sprint 3","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Sprint 1","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 1"}},"content":"**From**: 2025-10-28\\n\\n**To**: 2025-11-18\\n\\n**Scrum Master**: Marta Cruz\\n\\n**Product Owner**: IEETA\\n\\n**Developers**: Mariana Marques, Beatriz Francisco, Matilde Rodrigues, Catarina Ribeiro\\n\\nIn this sprint, we aimed to finish all the tasks that were not possible to complete in the previous sprint and since we had already completed most of the goals for milestone 2 in the previous sprint, we also started to advance work towards milestone 3:\\n\\n- UI Mockups\\n- Technology Stack\\n- Schemas and Models for all Databases\\n- Script to generate sensor data\\n- Setup all Frontend\\n- Update Microsite\\n- Update all the documentation\\n- Preparation for Second Presentation\\n\\n| Expected     | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 8        |\\n| Story Points | 40       |\\n\\n## Sprint Backlog\\n\\n| Task (KAN-\\\\*) | Description                 | Developer                                      | State | Story Points |\\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------ |\\n| KAN-9         | UI Mockups                  | Catarina Ribeiro                               | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-10        | Technologies                | Marta Cruz                                     | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-11        | Update Documentation        | All                                            | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-13        | Schemas and Models for all Databases | Marta Cruz and Mariana Marques        | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-14        | Script to generate sensor data | Beatriz Francisco and Matilde Rodrigues     | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-15        | Setup all Frontend          | Mariana Marques and Catarina Ribeiro           | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-16        | Update Microsite            | Catarina Ribeiro                               | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-17        | Preparation for Second Presentation | Matilde Rodrigues and Beatriz Francisco   | Done  | 5            |\\n\\n### Task Status (Completed/Not Completed)\\n\\n- [x] KAN-9: UI Mockups\\n- [x] KAN-10: Technologies\\n- [x] KAN-11: Update Documentation\\n- [x] KAN-13: Schemas and Models for all Databases\\n- [x] KAN-14: Script to generate sensor data\\n- [x] KAN-15: Setup all Frontend\\n- [x] KAN-16: Update Microsite\\n- [x] KAN-17: Preparation for Second Presentation\\n\\n## Sprint Review\\n\\n| Concluded    | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 8        |\\n| Story Points | 40       |\\n\\n## Sprint Retrospective\\n\\nIn this sprint, we managed to complete all the tasks that were planned. The team worked well together and managed to finish the sprint goals on time.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e`"},{"id":"Sprint 1","metadata":{"permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 1","source":"@site/blog/sprint1/sprint_1.md","title":"Sprint 1","description":"From: 2025-09-29","date":"2025-10-19T22:57:07.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"Sprint 1","title":"Sprint 1"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Sprint 2","permalink":"/microsite/blog/Sprint 2"}},"content":"**From**: 2025-09-29\\n\\n**To**: 2025-10-28\\n\\n**Scrum Master**: Mariana Marques\\n\\n**Product Owner**: IEETA\\n\\n**Developers**: Marta Cruz, Beatriz Francisco, Matilde Rodrigues, Catarina Ribeiro\\n## Sprint Goal\\n\\nIn order to complete the first milestone of our project, it is expectable to conclude the following sprints goals:\\n\\n- Functional requirements\\n- Non-functional requirements\\n- Personas\\n- Use Cases\\n- User Stories\\n- UI Mockups\\n- Architecture and Design\\n- Technology Stack\\n- State of the Art\\n- Creat Microsite\\n- Update all the documentation\\n- Presentation Preparation\\n\\n| Expected     | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 12       |\\n| Story Points | 60       |\\n\\n## Sprint Backlog\\n\\n| Task (KAN-\\\\*) | Description                 | Developer                                      | State | Story Points |\\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----- | ------------ |\\n| KAN-1         | State of the Art            | Beatriz Francisco                              | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-2         | Functional Requirements     | Mariana Marques                                | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-3         | Non-functional Requirements | Mariana Marques                                | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-4         | Personas                    | All                                            | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-5         | Use Cases                   | Mariana Marques and Beatriz Francisco          | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-6         | User Stories                | Matilde Rodrigues and Mariana Marques          | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-7         | Architecture and design     | Marta Cruz                                     | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-8         | Creat Microsite             | Catarina Ribeiro                               | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-9         | UI Mockups                  | Marta Cruz and Catarina Ribeiro                | Not Done  | 5        |\\n| KAN-10        | Technologies                | All                                            | Not Done  | 5        |\\n| KAN-11        | Update Documentation        | All                                            | Done  | 5            |\\n| KAN-12        | Presentation Preparatiion   | Matilde Rodrigues, Beatriz Francisco and Catarina Ribeiro  | Done  | 5  |\\n\\n### Task Status (Completed/Not Completed)\\n\\n- [x] KAN-1: State of the Art\\n- [x] KAN-2: Functional Requirements\\n- [x] KAN-3: Non-functional Requirements\\n- [x] KAN-4: Personas and \\n- [x] KAN-5: Use Cases\\n- [x] KAN-6: User Stories\\n- [x] KAN-7: Architecture\\n- [x] KAN-8: Creat Microsite\\n- [ ] KAN-9: UI Mockups\\n- [ ] KAN-10: Technologies\\n- [x] KAN-11: Update Documentation\\n- [x] KAN-12: Presentation Preparatiion\\n\\n## Sprint Review\\n\\n| Concluded    | Quantity |\\n| ------------ | -------- |\\n| Tasks        | 10       |\\n| Story Points | 50       |\\n\\n## Sprint Retrospective\\n\\nThis sprint saw substantial completion of tasks including UI mockups and updating project documentation. However, not all mockups were finalized, as only a few were required at this stage to support ongoing development. The remaining mockups will be created in future sprints as the design evolves and additional features are defined. Deciding which technologies to use was also delayed due to limited time and the need to prioritize other critical development tasks. Moving forward, the team plans to dedicate more time to technologies and design updates in upcoming sprints to ensure all project materials remain complete and aligned with progress.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e`"}]}}')}}]);